# Pads before a nested composite where the offset is always unaligned but by an amount only known at runtime, and
# pads by a constant amount at the end. The last field straddles a byte boundary so the bits above it in the final
# byte are not cleared by the write of the field itself. See https://github.com/OpenCyphal/nunavut/issues/397
uint1 x
uint2[<=1] y
VoidPadding.0.1 inner
uint3 z
uint7 w
@sealed
